---
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About"
  description="Learn what the District 10 Youth Leadership Coalition does and which organizational details are being confirmed."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="About D10YLC"
    title="Built for youth voice and civic action."
    intro="The District 10 Youth Leadership Coalition is a space for young people to learn, collaborate, and contribute to their community."
  />

  <section class="section section-teal">
    <div class="content-shell card-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="tag">Learn</span>
        <h2>Understand local government</h2>
        <p>
          Members explore how community priorities become public decisions and
          how youth can participate constructively.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="tag">Contribute</span>
        <h2>Bring lived experience</h2>
        <p>
          Young people notice needs and possibilities adults may miss. D10YLC
          creates a place to develop and communicate those perspectives.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="tag">Grow</span>
        <h2>Practice leadership</h2>
        <p>
          Projects create opportunities to listen, plan with others, speak
          clearly, and follow through on shared work.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">What is confirmed</p>
      <h2>A youth leadership coalition focused on San Jose District 10.</h2>
      <p>
        This first site version intentionally does not publish a student roster,
        meeting commitment, school eligibility rule, or council-office
        affiliation statement. The legacy site contains conflicting versions of
        those facts, and the current wording must come from D10YLC’s designated
        adult and editorial owners.
      </p>
      <div class="notice">
        <strong>Details under review</strong>
        Eligibility, current leadership, meeting cadence, term expectations,
        adult oversight, and the precise official relationship will be added
        after annual verification and any required consent.
      </div>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Who can join?</summary>
          <p>
            Current grade, school, residence, and service-area requirements are
            being confirmed. The Join page will become the single source of
            truth when approved.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How much time does participation take?</summary>
          <p>
            The current meeting cadence and expected commitment have not yet
            been verified. No applicant should rely on older versions of this
            information.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Who supervises the coalition?</summary>
          <p>
            Advisor and council-office relationship details will be published
            only after the responsible office approves the exact wording.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Why is there no student roster?</summary>
          <p>
            Names, schools, portraits, and biographies require current
            verification and appropriate consent. Privacy comes before a team
            directory.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
